{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788273522,"nonce":"bSMDIR5/e9Gm1Jmmp9jkk27JweY=","message":"IMPLEMENTED on branch `spec/site-routine`, commit `edfee42`. Session 15, worker.\nBuilds clean (`dotnet build -c Release`, 0/0). NOT bench-verified — a worker\nlaunches nothing; the orchestrator owns acceptance.\n\n\n`DevVerbs.WhyNoSpawn` returns `NoSpawn {Tier, Cell, Thing, Reason}` instead of a\nstring. Every failure row now carries `cell` (the cell that refused) and\n`cell_role` (its tier) beside the unchanged `at`, which stays the caller's own\nargument echoed back. `Blockers.At` gained an optional `known` Thing that beats\nits cell scan, because the scan answers \"what is on this cell\" and the game's\npredicate answers \"what did I object to\" — for `InteractionCellStandable` those\ndiffer when an unstandable blueprint sits under an edifice.\n\nThe branch reconstructions are the game's own walks repeated for the cell and\nthe thing the `AcceptanceReport` names only by label:\n\n- interaction: `ThingUtility.InteractionCellsWhenAt` then\n  `InteractionCellStandable`'s two predicates in its order (`passability !=\n  Standable || def == thingDef`, then the same against `entityDefToBuild`).\n- terrain: the first failing cell of the occupied rect, walked the way\n  `GenConstruct.CanBuildOnTerrain` walks it — rect clipped inside the map,\n  affordance from `ThingUtility.GetTerrainAffordanceNeed`, `IntVec3.GetAffordances`\n  (which prefers `TerrainGrid.FoundationAt`). `stuffDef` is null because\n  `GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt` itself passes none; that vanilla quirk is reproduced, not\n  corrected, since the job is to name the branch the game took.\n- footprint / bounds: as the issue describes.\n\n`ThingUtility.InteractionCellsWhenAt` returns the SHARED static\n`tmpInteractionCells`, cleared and refilled per call, so it is copied before\nanything else can call it. Recorded in the code.\n\n\nTwo branches the Scope did not know about, and one of them was a real defect.\n\n**`GenConstruct.NotBlockingAnyInteractionCells` runs inside `GenSpawn.CanSpawnAt`\nas well as inside `CanPlaceBlueprintAt`, and `WhyNoSpawn` never reproduced it.**\nSo a placement refused for covering a NEIGHBOUR's interaction cell fell through\nto the residual and was reported as \"ThingDef.CanSpawnAt refused\" — the wrong\nbranch, and no cell at all. That is this issue's own defect one level up: a\nrefusal describing something other than what refused. Verified member by member\nagainst `Verse/GenSpawn.cs CanSpawnAt`, which has SEVEN conditions\n(`ThingDef.CanSpawnAt`, `InBounds`, `Walkable`, the wipe scan, `CanBuildOnTerrain`,\n`InteractionCellStandable`, `NotBlockingAnyInteractionCells`) plus an eighth\n(`!canWipeEdifices \u0026\u0026 edificeGrid[item] != null`) unreachable from `dev:spawn-thing`,\nwhich passes `canWipeEdifices:true`. The file comment said six.\n\nTiers are therefore `bounds | footprint | terrain | interaction |\nblocks-interaction | def | place-search`. Kept apart rather than folded into the\nfour because each is a different REMEDY: `blocks-interaction` is cleared by\nmoving OUR building and never by clearing the cell it names, `def` names no cell,\nand `place-search` is the honest answer when `CanSpawnAt` accepted the target and\n`GenPlace` still found nowhere (the Near arm, and Direct for an item the cell's\nitem limit turned away). Both acceptance values the issue asserts —\n`interaction` and `footprint` — are unchanged.\n\n\n- Replay / target-is-rock / non-centre-terrain bullets: implemented, bench-owned.\n- `accept/s13-mod-surface.py` phase 1 shapes still pass by construction (the\n  three assertions that key on `blocker.refused` were preserved deliberately:\n  1.3p compares it to the full Near sentence, 1.5e to the clause, 1.6i requires\n  the sentence to END with the clause — the Near arm sets the row's `reason`\n  after `FailureRow` for exactly that).\n- Added: **1.3s-u** (`cell` echoes the target and `cell_role` is `place-search`\n  when no branch refused), **1.5h-j** (`cell` shape, `cell_role` one-of, and\n  `cell != at` on the interaction tier — the defect proper), **1.6l-m** (the two\n  new keys are in the JOURNAL ROW, not only the response). `--selftest` 25/25.\n\nDESIGN decisions log carries the `NotBlockingAnyInteractionCells` finding.","files":null}]}